Change 'The source design uses deep indigo for headers and primary actions, amber for highlights, paper white for backgrounds, green for success, and red for errors. The wireframes retain these visual roles. Their sample names and example study titles illustrate screen content rather than additional DefendIt features.' 'The implemented palette is teal #176B63, dark teal #103C3B, pale sage #E3F1ED, amber #E9B65E, paper #F4F7F5, white #FFFFFF, ink #18332F, muted #60756F, border #DCE6E0, success #287B57, and error #C34848. Legacy indigo identifiers now store teal hues. Figures illustrate layouts rather than live screenshots.'
Change 'This publication uses Century Gothic throughout. The source describes Source Serif 4 headings and Inter body text inside the application; the diagrams below use Century Gothic to meet the publication typography requirement.' 'The app uses Inter throughout: headings 30/22, titles 16, body 14, captions 12, and buttons 15 logical pixels. This document uses Century Gothic. Login shows DefendIt; MaterialApp.title and Strings.appName still say ThesisTrack.'
Change 'Rounded cards, status chips, bottom sheets, progress bars, and a sync chip form the main component set. Loading, empty, error, and validation states are part of each relevant flow.' 'Cards use a 20-pixel radius, inputs and primary buttons 14, and sheet tops 28 logical pixels. Primary buttons are at least 52 high. Loading, empty, error, and validation states support the workflows.'
Change 'The first two wireframes show entry into the application. Sign-in establishes identity; role setup collects the details needed to use the student or adviser workflow.' 'Sign-in establishes identity; role setup registers adviser credentials or a student number. Onboarding, then /home, follows the authentication state; the four tabs preserve state in an IndexedStack.'
Change 'The Today dashboard prioritizes the next consultation and work needing attention. Counts summarize the user''s groups and consultation availability. The sync chip communicates whether local work is offline, uploading, or synchronized; it is not an adviser-approval indicator.' 'Today combines Firestore group and slot streams with a SQLite Needs attention list. Students see revision, polish, overdue, and ready-to-submit items; advisers see pending reviews and overdue work. A pending count is not proof of successful remote delivery.'
Change 'The Title ideas screen separates the proposed title, description, and purpose from the review result. Approved, Needs polish, and Rejected are adviser decisions. Feedback tells the group what needs to change before another review.' 'Title states are pending, approved, needsPolish, and rejected. Members edit pending or needsPolish ideas and delete nonapproved ideas. Editing resets status to pending and clears review fields. Only the assigned adviser reviews; polish and rejection require feedback.'
Change 'The example title ideas in Figure 4.4 are sample thesis topics entered by a group. They do not expand DefendIt''s scope into attendance tracking. DefendIt''s function is to manage their submission and review.' 'Approved title ideas do not overwrite groups.thesisTitle or automatically approve the title_approval milestone. The example study titles are sample group content.'
Change 'The adviser preview brings together a group''s section, thesis topic, roster, and proposed titles before acceptance. It supports the adviser-request workflow described in Section 3.1, including the limit of four accepted groups.' 'The preview reads up to three proposals directly from Firestore. Acceptance transactionally sets adviserUid/adviserName and increments users.adviserGroupCount, rejecting an already assigned group or a count of four.'
Change 'The milestone task screen shows the milestone status, task completion, due date, assignees, and team workload. Students submit a milestone only after its tasks meet the submission conditions. Adviser approval remains separate from completing tasks.' 'The defaults are Title approval, Chapter 1 Introduction, Chapter 2 Review of Related Literature, Chapter 3 Methodology, Proposal defense, and Final defense. Their positions order the display; they do not enforce prerequisites between milestones.'
Change 'Status, completion counts, and feedback should be read together. A task progress bar describes work completed; a milestone approval records the adviser''s decision. Revisions return attention to the work that still needs to be addressed.' 'Students move notStarted to inProgress, then forReview; they may withdraw review or resubmit needsRevision. Advisers move forReview to approved or needsRevision. The first task starts work automatically. Overall progress averages 1 for approved milestones and done/total tasks otherwise, with zero for no tasks.'
Change 'The main packages are firebase_auth, google_sign_in, cloud_firestore, sqflite, provider, go_router, and connectivity_plus. SQLite provides per-user local storage, while Cloud Firestore distributes shared records through real-time listeners.' 'The declared Dart constraint is ^3.12.2; pubspec.lock requires Flutter >=3.44.0. Main packages are firebase_core ^4.15.0, firebase_auth ^6.7.0, google_sign_in ^7.2.0, cloud_firestore ^6.10.0, sqflite ^2.4.4+1, provider ^6.1.5+1, go_router ^17.5.0, and connectivity_plus ^7.3.2.'
Change 'The diagram shows the source''s entity fields. Profile and registration timestamps use Firestore server timestamps; operational date fields such as startsAt, dueAt, and updatedAt use integer milliseconds since the Unix epoch. Lists and maps retain their Firestore types; local serialization is described in Section 6.3.' 'The diagram follows model payloads and repository writes. Document IDs are separate from most payloads; users also store uid. createdAt on profiles and number claims, and claimedAt on code claims, are Firestore server timestamps. Other date fields are integer epoch milliseconds. Nullable fields are marked ?; lists and maps retain their Firestore types.'
Change 'Each signed-in user has a file named thesistrack_{uid}.db. Tables are consultations, action_items, title_ideas, milestones, milestone_tasks, and outbox. The outbox holds changes waiting to be sent to Firestore. Local identifiers are TEXT primary keys; done is stored as 0 or 1, and the consultation roster is JSON text locally rather than a Firestore list.' 'SQLite version 4 uses thesistrack_{uid}.db with consultations, action_items, title_ideas, milestones, milestone_tasks, and outbox. Mirrored records add id TEXT PRIMARY KEY; done becomes 0/1 and consultation roster becomes JSON TEXT. outbox uses an integer sequence. No SQL foreign keys or cascades are declared. Users, groups, slots, and registration registries have no dedicated SQLite tables.'
Change '1. Create a Firebase project and register an Android app with the application''s package name. Enable Google in Authentication.' '1. Use the configured project thesis-track-6a918 or an authorized replacement. Register Android package com.example.thesis_track and enable Google authentication.'
