Change 'One-time roles are adviser or student. Advisers enter an issued code (CPE-XXXX-XXXX); the profile and claim are saved in one transaction. Students register a unique student number and may enter a teammate code to join a group during sign-up.' 'Stored roles are adviser and student; leader is group metadata. Adviser onboarding formats an issued code such as CPE-2026-XXXX. Registration uppercases it, removes whitespace, rejects /, and transactionally claims the existing document. Another UID cannot reuse a claimed code; the same UID can.'
Change 'Student numbers use a four-digit year beginning with 20 and six further digits, displayed as 202X-XXXXXX. Sessions persist across restarts; sign-out clears Google and Firebase sessions.' 'Student numbers normalize to ten digits with a dash and match ^20\d{2}-\d{6}$. A transaction reserves studentNumbers/{number} for one UID. A teammate code is optional; joining failure after registration leaves the profile saved and shows retry guidance.'
Change 'Rules restrict profile access, protect identity fields, and authorize group records by membership or assigned adviser. Students cannot approve milestones or review titles. Tasks lock while a milestone is under review or approved. These are required backend policies; their deployed enforcement must be tested, including the limits noted in Section 10.1.' 'Repositories guard title and milestone membership and assigned-adviser actions. Consultation save/add/delete methods have no actor parameter and rely on UI restrictions plus backend rules. Required Firestore policies include ownership, membership, protected identity fields, review permissions, and task locks. No rule file is supplied, so deployed enforcement cannot be confirmed from this repository.'
Change 'SQLite stores local records, Cloud Firestore stores shared records, and the sync service connects them. Push saves a local change and its outbox operation in one SQLite transaction, then replays operations oldest first. Updates send changed fields; new records need their full payload. Failed operations remain queued for a later retry.' 'SQLite saves each local workflow change and its outbox entry in one transaction. outbox fields are seq INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, collection TEXT, docId TEXT, op TEXT, data TEXT?, and createdAt INTEGER. data is JSON; op is upsert or delete. collection can be a nested group path. The queue is not a Firestore collection.'
Change 'Pull uses Firestore listeners to update SQLite and refresh screens. Incoming changes do not replace a record with pending local edits; otherwise updatedAt determines whether an older incoming value is retained or applied. Device-clock ordering is a limitation, not guaranteed conflict resolution.' 'Flush replays seq order using Firestore merge writes or deletes, removing an entry only after success. Each push has a 12-second timeout. Failures retain the operation and block later entries for that attempt. Retry is triggered by writes, connectivity events, shell startup, or the sync chip; there is no dedicated backoff scheduler.'
Change 'Loaded notes, action items, titles, milestones, and tasks work offline. Sign-in, group coordination, slot changes, booking, and initial consultation opening need internet. Today combines local and remote data, so its entire view is not guaranteed offline. The chip shows Offline, Syncing, or Synced; tapping it requests sync when connected.' 'Listeners pull titles, milestones, and tasks by group. Advisers query consultations and actions by adviserUid; students query groupId. Pending local edits suppress incoming changes for that document. Otherwise a newer local updatedAt blocks an older update; equal timestamps can replace local data. Removed documents are deleted unless locally pending. This is not server-enforced conflict resolution.'
